    "summary": "Shark-tooth knife, maripi. Wooden knife with seven shark teeth: upper half carved as openwork manaia figure with haliotis-shell eyes, similar eyes in secondary manaia head in in-curved back of main figure; surface decoration of unaunahi and pungawerewere. End of handle as simplified, very worn face with terminal loop through which leather suspension cord is threaded. Surface ornamentation very worn. Teeth are inserted into groove in front of main manaia and fixed with resin (?); no lashing.",
